description:
As a Junior Product Information Administrator, you will play an important role in maintaining and improving product information within our Product Information Management (PIM) system. You will make sure that product descriptions, attributes, images and documents are accurate, complete and ready to be used across our different channels.




 This is a great opportunity for someone who is curious, eager to learn and enjoys working with data. You don't need to know everything from day one, are looking for someone who wants to develop their skills and grow with us




**Responsibilities**
 You will work closely with colleagues, suppliers and internal stakeholders to collect, maintain and improve product information. Your responsibilities will include:




* Maintain and update product information in our PIM system, including descriptions, attributes, images and documents.
* Ensure data quality by checking product information for accuracy, completeness and consistency and correcting errors or missing information.
* Collect and manage product information from suppliers and internal stakeholders, supporting the creation and publication of content for new products.
* Handle internal product information requests through our ticketing system and support colleagues with data-related questions.
* Support data standardization and harmonization initiatives to improve the overall quality and consistency of our product information.
* Maintain documentation and guidelines and follow established PIM processes and ways of working.
* Identify opportunities to improve processes and efficiency, including supporting automation initiatives where applicable.You will be part of a team where collaboration is important.


**What do we offer?**
 You will join a growing, international and well-established company where you can develop your skills and build a strong foundation for your career.




* A junior role with plenty of opportunity to learn and develop;
* A 1-year contract with the possibility of a permanent position;
* A salary indication of approximately SEK 30,000 per month depending on previous experience and skills;
* Hybrid position with a minimum of three days at the office;
* A position based in Solna, ideal for someone living in or around the Solna area;
* The opportunity to gain experience with PIM, e-commerce, rental systems and SAP;
* An international working environment with colleagues across different teams and countries;
* A varied role combining data, administration, systems and collaboration.


**Who are you?**
 This is a junior position, so we value your potential and willingness to learn just as much as your previous experience. You don't need to know everything from day one. We are looking for someone who is curious, structured and enjoys working with data and details.




**We Are Looking For Someone Who**
* Has completed secondary education or an equivalent level of education, preferably with a background in administration, business, IT or data management;
* Has good knowledge of Microsoft Office, especially Excel;
* Has some experience with data administration or product information. This can also be gained through an internship, education or an entry-level position;
* Works accurately and has a strong eye for detail and consistency;
* Is curious, eager to learn and able to organize tasks and priorities effectively;
* Enjoys working with different stakeholders and has a collaborative and customer-focused mindset;
* Is fluent in Swedish and English, both written and spoken.


 Låter tjänsten intressant?




 Om du tror att detta är jobbet för, skicka in din ansökan!
